      {
        "review_id": 301625955,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r301625955-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Must visit Pashupatinath Temple in Kathmandu. Nepal",
        "text": "On my way to Kailash Manasarover Yatra I had a two day stay in Kathmandu.i visited the pashupatinath Temple.The temple was erected in the 15 century by Lichhavi King.The richly ornamented pagoda houses the sacred Linga or holy symbol of shiva.Pashupatinath Temple is located on both banks of Bagmati River .The main temple of Pashupatinath is a building with a bunk roof and a golden spire.It is a cubic construction with four main door ,all covered with silver sheets. Only followers of hindusim can enter the main temple, But all the other bulding are available for foreigners to visit.Along the right bank of Bagmati river numerous platforms for funeral pyres are built.The cremations on these platforms are a common activity everyday.It is also very common to meet sadhus in pashupatinath temple.Sadhu are wandering ascetic yogis, who are trying to acquire liberation from the cycle of death rebirth by meditating.It is belived that those who die in Pashupatinath Temple are reborn asa human,regardless of any misconduct that could worsen their Karma.If you are attacted to the places where death can be felt,consider Pashupatinath as your first destination.It is a temple with special atmosphere of death, death is present in almost every ritual and every corner of it. OM NAMAH SHIVA.",
