        "title": "The Hindu Rome.",
        "text": "Construction started on this temple in the 7th century. It sits on the Bagmati river in Nepal and is one of the holiest sites in the hindu religion.The entire complex has 500+s other shrines and smaller temples. It is guarded by Nepalese  police. Pashupathinath admits only Hindus. it is encased with silver walls and has a gold pagoda roof The complex is a world heritage UNESCO site.  Gat's jut out into the Bagmati river.These are used by a dedicated cast to cremate the dead. Similar in fact to the use of the gats in city of Benares on the Ganges( India) The cremations are a sobering sight and the river looks polluted but this has been a center of the hindu faith for many centuries,as such  will remain for many more.",
        "review_tip": null,
