        "title": "Not what I expected",
        "text": "The first time I came here I was expecting a little bit more from this place. I heard it from a few travelers on what is done here, where families would come to burn the deceased members body and into the water. I visited with a friend and entered through the wrong entrance. We ended up watching the ceremony. The part I did not enjoy was seeing dozens of foreigners snapping photos of this from the distance. If it was my family I would hate people taking photos of this emotional time. Entrance fee was 1000 Nepali rupees too. quite high in my opinion. Average price for an attraction in Nepal for the entrance fee is usually 200-500 Rupees",
        "review_tip": null,
